Phasmid: CDP attachment is invisible to pages

What:     Describing values for a CDP client (console arguments, exceptions,
          previews) runs no page code and changes nothing a page reads later.
          Error name and message are read by descriptor, builtin getters only;
          the stack text comes from the frames captured at creation; previews
          skip "stack" and run builtin getters under V8's side-effect check.
          The protocol is unchanged; previews show fewer getter values.
          Console calls with a client attached remain slower.
Why:      With Runtime.enable on, stock V8 runs page getters for an error's
          name and message and formats its stack early, so a page can tell a
          CDP client is attached.
Profile:  none (unconditional; V8 cannot read the profile)
Hooks:    v8/src/inspector/value-mirror.cc getErrorProperty,
          descriptionForError, ValueMirror::getProperties,
          doesAttributeHaveObservableSideEffectOnGet
Contexts: main, iframe, worker, shared worker, service worker
Guard:    tests/guards/automation/cdp-stealth.py

